current system issues: 
No Authentication
Anyone can connect. No username. No password.
No Encryption
Messages travel in plain text. Anyone can read them.
No Authorization
Connected clients can publish or subscribe to any topic. There are no rules about who can access what — a guest could read sensor data meant for operations, or send commands meant only for administrators.
Default Port
Port 1883 is the standard MQTT port. Attackers know to check it.

mosquitto_sub -t "#" -v 
